      "form_guide": "",
      "comment": "JOYOH (4) brings the strongest recent form after chasing Linchpin home at Ascot in NMW1Y company, beaten 1.2L after leading and only being claimed late. The move back from Saturday company is ideal, and while 1650m is new territory, she can dictate proceedings and be tough to run down. DE LAGO'S ROCK (5) has an appealing profile with one win and three places from five starts, a strong 1650m record, and Pike staying aboard after a decisive Northam Mdn win. FINAL CALL (3) was only beaten two and a half lengths first-up in a small Northam field and has enough overall consistency on good tracks to be a genuine placing threat if sharper second-up. COSTA DEL DARLO (1) has form tying in through a couple of these and has to be respected.",
